messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 34197 and 55144?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 34,197 and 55,144. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts based on the place values of the digits in 55,144.\n\nStarting with the ones place, I'll multiply 34,197 by 4. This gives me 136,788.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 34,197 by the tens place digit, which is 40. This results in 1,367,880.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 34,197 by the hundreds place digit, 100, giving me 3,419,700.\n\nMoving on to the thousands place, I'll multiply 34,197 by 5,000, which equals 170,985,000.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 34,197 by the ten-thousands place digit, 50,000, resulting in 1,709,850,000.\n\nAfter obtaining all these partial products, I'll sum them up to find the final product.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
