messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 45065 and 20973?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n.\nFirst, I need to multiply 45065 by 20973. To make this easier, I'll break down 20973 into its place values: 20000, 900, 70, and 3.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 45065 by each of these components separately.\n\nStarting with 45065 multiplied by 3, which equals 135195.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 45065 by 70, resulting in 3154550.\n\nAfter that, multiplying 45065 by 900 gives me 40558500.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 45065 by 20000, which equals 901300000.\n\nNow, I'll add all these partial products together: 135195 + 3154550 + 40558500 + 901300000</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
