messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 92714 and 45123?\n# Reasoning:", '<think>\n\nFirst, I need to multiply 92714 by each digit of 45123, starting from the ones place and moving to the higher places.\n\n1. Multiply 92714 by 3 (the ones place of 45123):\n   92714 × 3 = 278,142\n\n2. Multiply 92714 by 20 (the tens place of 45123):\n   92714 × 20 = 1,854,280\n\n3. Multiply 92714 by 100 (the hundreds place of 45123):\n   92714 × 100 = 9,271,400\n\n4. Multiply 92714 by 5000 (the thousands place of 45123):\n   92714 × 5000 = 463,570,000\n\n5. Multiply 92714 by 40,000 (the ten-thousands place of 45123):\n   92714 × 40,000 = 3,708,560,000\n\nFinally, I will add all these partial products together to get the final result.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is ']]
