messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 10685 and 72966?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 10685 and 72966. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable steps.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 10685 by each digit of 72966, taking into account the place value of each digit. This means I'll multiply 10685 by 6 (units place), then by 60 (tens place), followed by 900 (hundreds place), 2000 (thousands place), and finally by 70000 (ten-thousands place).\n\nAfter performing each of these multiplications, I'll add up all the intermediate results to get the final product. This step-by-step approach ensures that I handle each part of the multiplication accurately and systematically.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
