      "text": "614,227,272.\n\n\\boxed{614227272}\n\n# Step-by-Step Explanation:\n\nTo find the product of **47,982** and **12,816**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n1. **Multiply 47,982 by 10,000:**\n   \\[\n   47,\\!982 \\times 10,\\!000 = 479,\\!820,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 47,982 by 2,000:**\n   \\[\n   47,\\!982 \\times 2,\\!000 = 95,\\!964,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 47,982 by 800:**\n   \\[\n   47,\\!982 \\times 800 = 38,\\!385,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 47,982 by 10:**\n   \\[\n   47,\\!982 \\times 10 = 479,\\!820\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 47,982 by 6:**\n   \\[\n   47,\\!982 \\times 6 = 287,\\!892\n   \\]\n\n6. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   479,\\!820,\\!000 + 95,\\!964,\\!000 + 38,\\!385,\\!600 + 479,\\!820 + 287,\\!892 = 614,\\!227,\\!272\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{614227272}\n\\]",
