messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 83318 and 10525?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to multiply 83,318 by 10,525. To make this easier, I'll break down 10,525 into its place values: 10,000, 500, 20, and 5.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 83,318 by each of these components separately.\n\nStarting with 10,000:\n83,318 multiplied by 10,000 is 833,180,000.\n\nThen, multiplying by 500:\n83,318 times 500 equals 41,659,000.\n\nNext, multiplying by 20:\n83,318 multiplied by 20 is 1,666,360.\n\nFinally, multiplying by 5:\n83,318 times 5 equals 416,590.\n\nAfter obtaining all these partial products, I'll add them together to find the final result.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
