messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 31600 and 81332?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n.\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 31,600 and 81,332. To make this easier, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 31,600 by each digit of 81,332, taking into account the place value of each digit.\n\nFirst, multiply 31,600 by 2 (the ones place):.\n31,600 × 2 = 63,200.\n\nNext, multiply 31,600 by 30 (the tens place):.\n31,600 × 30 = 948,000.\n\nThen, multiply 31,600 by 300 (the hundreds place):.\n31,600 × 300 = 9,480,000.\n\nAfter that, multiply 31,600 by 1,000 (the thousands place):.\n31,600 × 1,000 = 31,600,000.\n\nFinally, multiply 31,600 by 80,000 (the ten-thousands place):.\n31,600 × 80,000 = 2,528,000,000.\n\nNow, I'll add up all these partial products to get the final result:</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
