messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 79021 and 31303?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to multiply 79021 by 31303. To make this easier, I'll break down 31303 into its place values: 30000, 1000, 300, and 3.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 79021 by each of these components separately.\n\nStarting with 30000:\n79021 multiplied by 30000 is 2,370,630,000.\n\nThen, multiplying by 1000:\n79021 multiplied by 1000 is 79,021,000.\n\nNext, multiplying by 300:\n79021 multiplied by 300 is 23,706,300.\n\nFinally, multiplying by 3:\n79021 multiplied by 3 is 237,063.\n\nAfter obtaining all these partial products, I'll add them together to find the final result.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
