messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 19295 and 19847?\n# Reasoning:", '<think>\n\nFirst, I need to multiply 19295 by each digit of 19847, starting from the ones place and moving to the higher places.\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place (7):**\n   19295 × 7 = 135,065\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place (40):**\n   19295 × 40 = 771,800\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place (800):**\n   19295 × 800 = 15,436,000\n\n4. **Multiply by the thousands place (9,000):**\n   19295 × 9,000 = 173,655,000\n\n5. **Multiply by the ten-thousands place (10,000):**\n   19295 × 10,000 = 192,950,000\n\nFinally, I will add all these partial products together to get the final result.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is ']]
