messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 42710 and 45211?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to multiply 42710 by 45211. To make this easier, I'll break down 45211 into its place values: 40000, 5000, 200, 10, and 1.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 42710 by each of these components separately.\n\nStarting with 42710 multiplied by 40000, I'll calculate 42710 × 40000.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 42710 by 5000.\n\nAfter that, I'll multiply 42710 by 200.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 42710 by 10.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 42710 by 1.\n\nOnce I have all these partial products, I'll add them all together to get the final result.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
