messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 39984 and 87483?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 39,984 and 87,483. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into more manageable parts by considering each digit of the second number and its place value.\n\nStarting with the ones place, I'll multiply 39,984 by 3. This gives me 119,952.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 39,984 by 80, which is the tens place of 87,483. This results in 3,198,720.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 39,984 by 400, representing the hundreds place. This calculation yields 15,993,600.\n\nMoving on to the thousands place, I'll multiply 39,984 by 7,000, which equals 279,888,000.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 39,984 by 80,000, the ten-thousands place, resulting in 3,198,720,000.\n\nAfter obtaining all these partial products, I'll sum them up to find the total product.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
