      "text": "3,498,720,000.\n\n\\boxed{3498720000}\n\n# Step-by-Step Explanation:\n\nTo find the product of **39,984** and **87,483**, we'll break down the multiplication into manageable parts by considering each digit of the second number and its place value.\n\n1. **Multiply by the Ones Place (3):**\n   \\[\n   39,\\!984 \\times 3 = 119,\\!952\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the Tens Place (80):**\n   \\[\n   39,\\!984 \\times 80 = 3,\\!198,\\!720\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the Hundreds Place (400):**\n   \\[\n   39,\\!984 \\times 400 = 15,\\!993,\\!600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply by the Thousands Place (7,000):**\n   \\[\n   39,\\!984 \\times 7,\\!000 = 279,\\!888,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply by the Ten-Thousands Place (80,000):**\n   \\[\n   39,\\!984 \\times 80,\\!000 = 3,\\!198,\\!720,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n6. **Sum All the Partial Products:**\n   \\[\n   119,\\!952 + 3,\\!198,\\!720 + 15,\\!993,\\!600 + 279,\\!888,\\!000 + 3,\\!198,\\!720,\\!000 = 3,\\!498,\\!720,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{3498720000}\n\\]",
