messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 81116 and 17486?\n# Reasoning:", '<think>\n\nFirst, I need to multiply 81116 by each digit of 17486, starting from the ones place and moving to the higher places.\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place (6):**\n   81116 × 6 = 486,696\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place (80):**\n   81116 × 80 = 6,489,280\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place (400):**\n   81116 × 400 = 32,446,400\n\n4. **Multiply by the thousands place (7,000):**\n   81116 × 7,000 = 567,812,000\n\n5. **Multiply by the ten-thousands place (10,000):**\n   81116 × 10,000 = 811,160,000\n\nFinally, I will add all these partial products together to get the final result.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is ']]
