      "text": "844,625,253.\n\n# Solution:\n\nTo find the product of **29603** and **28551**, we'll break down the multiplication step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nLet's express **28551** in terms of its place values:\n\\[\n28551 = 20000 + 8000 + 500 + 50 + 1\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Multiply Each Component\nNow, multiply **29603** by each component of **28551**:\n\n1. **Multiply by 20000:**\n\\[\n29603 \\times 20000 = 29603 \\times 2 \\times 10000 = 59206 \\times 10000 = 592,\\!060,\\!000\n\\]\n\n2. **Multiply by 8000:**\n\\[\n29603 \\times 8000 = 29603 \\times 8 \\times 1000 = 236,\\!824 \\times 1000 = 236,\\!824,\\!000\n\\]\n\n3. **Multiply by 500:**\n\\[\n29603 \\times 500 = 29603 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 148,\\!015 \\times 100 = 14,\\!801,\\!500\n\\]\n\n4. **Multiply by 50:**\n\\[\n29603 \\times 50 = 29603 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 148,\\!015 \\times 10 = 1,\\!480,\\!150\n\\]\n\n5. **Multiply by 1:**\n\\[\n29603 \\times 1 = 29,\\!603\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Sum All the Products\nNow, add all the results from the previous step:\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n592,\\!060,\\!000 \\\\\n+ 236,\\!824,\\!000 \\\\\n+ 14,\\!801,\\!500 \\\\\n+ 1,\\!480,\\!150 \\\\\n+ 29,\\!603 \\\\\n\\hline\n844,\\!625,\\!253 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\\[\n\\boxed{844,\\!625,\\!253}\n\\]",
