messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 14630 and 31001?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n.\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 14,630 and 31,001. To make this easier, I'll break down 31,001 into its place values: 30,000, 1,000, and 1.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 14,630 by each of these components separately. .\n\nFirst, multiplying 14,630 by 30,000 gives me 438,900,000.\n\nThen, multiplying 14,630 by 1,000 results in 14,630,000.\n\nFinally, multiplying 14,630 by 1 gives me 14,630.\n\nAfter obtaining these individual products, I'll add them all together to find the total product</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
