messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 84620 and 11732?\n# Reasoning:", '<think>\n\nFirst, I need to multiply 84620 by each digit of 11732, starting from the ones place and moving to the higher places.\n\n1. **Multiply by the ones place (2):**\n   84620 × 2 = 169240\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place (30):**\n   84620 × 30 = 2,538,600\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place (700):**\n   84620 × 700 = 59,234,000\n\n4. **Multiply by the thousands place (1000):**\n   84620 × 1000 = 84,620,000\n\n5. **Multiply by the ten-thousands place (10,000):**\n   84620 × 10,000 = 846,200,000\n\nFinally, I will add all these partial products together to get the final result.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is ']]
