messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 18168 and 56523?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 18,168 and 56,523. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable steps.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 18,168 by each digit of 56,523, taking into account the place value of each digit. This means I'll multiply by 3 (ones place), 20 (tens place), 500 (hundreds place), 6,000 (thousands place), and 50,000 (ten-thousands place).\n\nAfter performing each of these multiplications, I'll add up all the intermediate results to get the final product.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
