      "text": "1,025,000,000.\n\n\\boxed{1025000000}\n\n# Step-by-Step Explanation:\n\nTo find the product of **18,168** and **56,523**, we'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable steps.\n\n1. **Multiply 18,168 by 3 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   18,168 \\times 3 = 54,504\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 18,168 by 20 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   18,168 \\times 20 = 363,360\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 18,168 by 500 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   18,168 \\times 500 = 9,084,000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 18,168 by 6,000 (thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   18,168 \\times 6,000 = 109,008,000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 18,168 by 50,000 (ten-thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   18,168 \\times 50,000 = 908,400,000\n   \\]\n\n6. **Add all the results together:**\n   \\[\n   54,504 + 363,360 + 9,084,000 + 109,008,000 + 908,400,000 = 1,025,000,000\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{1025000000}\n\\]",
