messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 20748 and 68334?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 20748 and 68334. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts based on the place value of each digit in 68334.\n\nStarting with the ones place, I'll multiply 20748 by 4. This gives me 82,992.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 20748 by the tens place digit, which is 30. This results in 622,440.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 20748 by the hundreds place digit, 300, yielding 6,224,400.\n\nMoving on to the thousands place, multiplying 20748 by 8,000 gives me 165,984,000.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 20748 by the ten-thousands place digit, 60,000, which equals 1,244,880,000.\n\nAfter obtaining all these partial products, I'll sum them up to find the final product.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
