messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 11299 and 48118?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 11,299 and 48,118. To do this, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more manageable parts based on the place value of each digit in 48,118.\n\nStarting with the ones place, I'll multiply 11,299 by 8. This gives me 90,392.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 11,299 by 100, which is the tens place of 48,118. This results in 1,129,900.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 11,299 by 1,000, corresponding to the hundreds place, yielding 11,299,000.\n\nMoving on to the thousands place, I'll multiply 11,299 by 8,000, which equals 90,392,000.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 11,299 by 40,000, the ten-thousands place, resulting in 451,960,000.\n\nAfter obtaining all these partial products, I'll sum them up to find the total product.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
