      "text": "8,433,223,620.\n\n\\boxed{8433223620}\n\n# Step-by-Step Explanation:\n\nTo find the product of **98,460** and **85,477**, we'll break down the multiplication into manageable steps by considering each digit of **85,477** and its place value.\n\n1. **Multiply 98,460 by 7 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!460 \\times 7 = 689,\\!220\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 98,460 by 70 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!460 \\times 70 = 6,\\!892,\\!200\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 98,460 by 400 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!460 \\times 400 = 39,\\!384,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 98,460 by 5,\\!000 (thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!460 \\times 5,\\!000 = 492,\\!300,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 98,460 by 80,\\!000 (ten-thousands place):**\n   \\[\n   98,\\!460 \\times 80,\\!000 = 7,\\!876,\\!800,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n6. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   689,\\!220 + 6,\\!892,\\!200 + 39,\\!384,\\!000 + 492,\\!300,\\!000 + 7,\\!876,\\!800,\\!000 = 8,\\!433,\\!223,\\!620\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{8433223620}\n\\]",
