messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 32707 and 33536?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\n\nFirst, I need to calculate the product of 32,707 and 33,536. To make this manageable, I'll break down the multiplication into smaller, more straightforward steps.\n\nI'll start by multiplying 32,707 by each digit of 33,536, taking into account the place value of each digit. This means I'll handle the units, tens, hundreds, thousands, and ten-thousands places separately.\n\nAfter obtaining each partial product, I'll add them all together to get the final result. This step-by-step approach ensures accuracy and makes the multiplication process more organized.\n</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
