      "text": "1,096,332,  32707 multiplied by 33536 equals 1,096,332.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Multiply 32,707 by 6 (units place of 33,536):**\n   \\[\n   32,707 \\times 6 = 196,242\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 32,707 by 30 (tens place of 33,536):**\n   \\[\n   32,707 \\times 30 = 981,210\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 32,707 by 500 (hundreds place of 33,536):**\n   \\[\n   32,707 \\times 500 = 16,353,500\n   \\]\n\n4. **Multiply 32,707 by 3,000 (thousands place of 33,536):**\n   \\[\n   32,707 \\times 3,000 = 98,121,000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Multiply 32,707 by 30,000 (ten-thousands place of 33,536):**\n   \\[\n   32,707 \\times 30,000 = 981,210,000\n   \\]\n\n6. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   196,242 + 981,210 + 16,353,500 + 98,121,000 + 981,210,000 = 1,096,332,  32707 \\times 33536 = 1,096,332\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\\[\n\\boxed{1,\\!096,\\!332,\\!32707 \\times 33536 = 1,\\!096,\\!332}\n\\]",
